ops.body:
synckit implementation workflow wf_8c2b365b-522 complete: cc-sync/artifact-delivery @ ea6d2dfdcc81 (integration 4a2ef65 + review fixes 7c44f26 and ea6d2df). Of 9 review findings, 8 were fixed with regression tests and 1 rejected (out-of-scope LFS note).
Blockers fixed:
- An object was reported present before its write was durable; in-flight digests now read as absent.
- A manifest first reached as a blob never had its deps walked; the closure keeps separate emitted and expanded sets.
- An interrupted apply.v2 could leave receipted roots unpinned; union-then-narrow now runs on a single durable synckit.accepted/<origin> owner.
Majors and minors fixed:
- explicit ObjectEntry kinds end to end (no byte sniffing);
- pin validation at MaxPinRoots = 2×MaxRoots;
- delivery pins reconciled after a crash/restart;
- shared ref-counted outbox batches across lanes;
- committed/<id> records let concurrent senders finish.
Gates: build, vet, lint 0, go test -race -count=3 on artifact/syncservice/daemon.
Open items for the synckit final merge:
- accepted-pin growth across repeated failed applies (coordinator decision: pin set = prior acked roots ∪ current change roots, bounded);
- a narrow process-crash durability gap (decision: sync all object directories on Store Open);
- reconcile the speculative delta branch cc-sync/synckit-delta1 (D4/D5/D8/D9/D10 plus duplicate kind/pin-cap work, preferring the reviewed ea6d2df versions);
- a whole-diff astra review.
